# Geometry Button — a Skia button made of 50 rounded-rect rings: pressing springs
# the rings outward into a flower (path rebuilt every frame from progress) and
# scales the canvas 0.5 -> 1 with a heavy haptic; releasing logs "🪄".
# What this test covers: a quick tap (log), a long hold (fully expanded, then
# released), rapid repeated taps that reverse the spring mid-flight, a press that
# drags off the button before releasing, and a tap on the outer (scaled-down)
# area of the canvas.
# expect-log: 🪄
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/geometry-button"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 45000
# Warm-up touch on the status bar: the first touch of a test can be lost while
# the XCTest runner attaches.
press 330 20
wait 500
wait 1500
press 201 437
wait 1200
longpress 201 437 2500
wait 1200
press 201 437 --count 6 --interval-ms 120
wait 1500
# Hold, drag off the button and release outside.
gesture pan 201 437 170 0 1200
wait 1500
# Edge of the visible (0.5-scaled) canvas.
press 245 437
wait 1200
longpress 201 437 600
wait 1500
wait "label=\"Close\"" 15000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
